<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The final weeks the UT graduate’s first solo show features larger-than-life sculptures that pokes fun and shows his admiration for his home state.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Through Sept. 13, Midland, <a href="http://www.museumsw.org/ken-womack">www.museumsw.org/ken-womack</a></p>
</div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" width="780" height="520" data-attachment-id="466859" data-permalink="https://www.austinchronicle.com/columns/day-trips-beyond-september-events-roundup/attachment/sept7_museum-big-bend/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?fit=1800%2C1200&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1800,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-title="Sept7_Museum Big Bend" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;The Museum of the Big Bend in Alpine brings together artists and craftsmen for an annual show and sale.&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?fit=780%2C520&amp;ssl=1" src="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=780%2C520&#038;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-466859" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=1200%2C800&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=550%2C367&amp;ssl=1 550w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=800%2C533&amp;ssl=1 800w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=780%2C520&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?resize=400%2C267&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend.jpg?w=1800&amp;ssl=1 1800w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept7_Museum-Big-Bend-1024x683.jpg?w=370&amp;ssl=1 370w" sizes="(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">The Museum of the Big Bend in Alpine brings together artists and craftsmen for an annual show and sale. <span class="image-credit"><span class="credit-label-wrapper">Credit:</span> Gerald E. McLeod</span></figcaption></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Trappings of Texas&nbsp;</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Celebrating the rich culture and craftsmanship of the American West, this exhibit and sale features work from premier artists and custom equipment makers. The exhibit will remain on display at the museum through Oct. 31.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 17-19, Alpine, <a href="http://www.museumofthebigbend.com">www.museumofthebigbend.com</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Telescope 101 Workshop</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Who better to teach you the basics of that telescope sitting in a box in your closet or help you decide which telescope to buy than the experts at McDonald Observatory? Get hands-on instructions to better understand how optics work and how to find your way around the night sky under some of the darkest skies in the U.S. BYOT or use theirs.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 23, Fort Davis, <a href="https://mcdonaldobservatory.org/visit/telescopes-101/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">mcdonaldobservatory.org/visit/telescopes-101</a></p>
</div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>GULF COAST</strong></h2>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Galveston Island Wine Festival &nbsp;</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Celebrity, regional, and local chefs join this annual event featuring wine tastings, gourmet culinary experiences, and live entertainment in a tropical setting. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 4-6, Galveston, <a href="http://www.visitgalveston.com/events/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">www.visitgalveston.com/events</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Open Days at the Garden</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Join a tour of the John Fairey Garden’s more than 5,000 plants from Mexico, Asia, and the U.S. at 10am, 11am, and 1pm. The nursery will be open from 9-3.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 12, Hempstead, <a href="https://jfgarden.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">jfgarden.org</a></p>
</div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" width="780" height="520" data-attachment-id="466860" data-permalink="https://www.austinchronicle.com/columns/day-trips-beyond-september-events-roundup/attachment/sept8_bolivar-lighthouse/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?fit=1800%2C1200&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1800,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-title="Sept8_Bolivar Lighthouse" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;Take a look inside the Bolivar Point Lighthouse, a ferry ride from Galveston.&lt;/p&gt;
" data-large-file="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?fit=780%2C520&amp;ssl=1" src="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=780%2C520&#038;ssl=1" alt="" class="wp-image-466860" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=1024%2C683&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=1200%2C800&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=550%2C367&amp;ssl=1 550w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=800%2C533&amp;ssl=1 800w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=780%2C520&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?resize=400%2C267&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse.jpg?w=1800&amp;ssl=1 1800w, https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept8_Bolivar-Lighthouse-1024x683.jpg?w=370&amp;ssl=1 370w" sizes="(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Take a look inside the Bolivar Point Lighthouse, a ferry ride from Galveston. <span class="image-credit"><span class="credit-label-wrapper">Credit:</span> Gerald E. McLeod</span></figcaption></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bolivar Point Lighthouse Open House</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is a rare opportunity to see up close the restoration work being done on the historic 1872 lighthouse.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 13, Port Bolivar, <a href="https://bolivarpointlighthouse.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">bolivarpointlighthouse.org</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Galveston Sandcastle Festival  &nbsp;</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Houston-area architects, designers, engineers, and contractors take their tools to Galveston’s East Beach for what is considered one of the world’s largest amateur sandcastle competitions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 19-20, Galveston,&nbsp;<a href="https://www.visitgalveston.com/events/annual-events/galveston-sandcastle-competition">www.visitgalveston.com</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Galveston Island Shrimp Festival &nbsp;</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Galveston Island is a seafood lover’s paradise all year, but in September it explodes with a little taste of heaven.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 25-26, Galveston, <a href="http://www.visitgalveston.com/events/?page=3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">www.visitgalveston.com/events</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Texas Food Championship</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chefs, pitmasters, and home cooks compete for a chance to represent the state in the World Food Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 25-27, Corpus Christi, <a href="http://www.texasfoodchampionship.com">www.texasfoodchampionship.com</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Red, White &amp; Beeville</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Walk among beautifully restored aircraft, purchase a ride in an authentic 1940s-era airplane, and explore emergency and specialty vehicles during the Touch-a-Truck experience.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 26, Beeville, <a href="https://members.experiencebeecounty.org/events" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">members.experiencebeecounty.org/events</a></p>
</div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>HILL COUNTRY</strong></h2>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“<strong>Houdini’s Library</strong>”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of history’s most famous illusionists, Harry Houdini also built an astounding personal collection of books, manuscripts, and ephemera documenting the long global history of magic and theatre that the Ransom Center acquired in 1958. Commemorating the centenary of Houdini’s death&nbsp;in 1926, this exhibit delves into the magician’s study of the world around him.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 1-Jan. 24, Austin, <a href="http://www.hrc.utexas.edu/exhibitions">www.hrc.utexas.edu/exhibitions</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>In a Pickle Festival</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Come enjoy pickle food, contests, shopping, games, and a carnival. Festival favorites include pickle eating contests, pickle juice drinking contests, a pet parade, and interactive activities for all ages.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 19-20, Helotes, <a href="https://inapicklefest.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">inapicklefest.com</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sweet Eats Farm Fall Festival</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Explore the 4.5-acre themed corn maze, and Texas-sized pumpkin patch, daily pig races, a petting zoo, pony rides, wagon rides, apple cannons, and over 30 exciting farm-themed activities.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 19-Nov. 8, Georgetown, <a href="http://www.sweeteats.com">www.sweeteats.com</a></p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4fc3f8e1 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Texas Music Festival</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Three evenings of cool country and blues music in Robinson City Park.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sept. 25-26, Llano, <a href="http://www.llanotexasmusicfest.com">www.llanotexasmusicfest.com</a></p>
</div>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-recalc-dims="1" decoding="async" width="780" height="520" data-attachment-id="466861" data-permalink="https://www.austinchronicle.com/columns/day-trips-beyond-september-events-roundup/attachment/sept9_oatmeal/" data-orig-file="https://i0.wp.com/www.austinchronicle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sept9_Oatmeal.jpg?fit=1800%2C1200&amp;ssl=1" data-orig-size="1800,1200" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-title="Sept9_Oatmeal" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="&lt;p&gt;Feel your oats at the annual Oatmeal Festival.&lt;/p&gt;
