<p>In babydoll dresses and bloomers, wearing flower crowns and carrying handheld fans, mother-daughter duos traipsed from one’s favorite band to the other’s. As Bikini Kill called for a revolution and Doechii sampled Beyoncé, they tied hopes and dreams to Yoko Ono’s Wish Tree and snapped photos in front of a hot-pink Jenny Holzer truism in [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.austinchronicle.com/music/live-shots/hopeful-and-resolved-olivia-rodrigos-daisy-chain-fields-festival-connects-women-of-all-ages/">Hopeful and Resolved, Olivia Rodrigo’s Daisy Chain Fields Festival Connects Women of All Ages </a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.austinchronicle.com">The Austin Chronicle</a>.</p>
